4x − 2y = 8', '["Exactly one", "Infinitely many", "Zero", "Exactly two"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'The second equation is 2 times the first, so the lines are the same.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2d_013', 'math', 2, 'Algebra', 'Systems of linear equations', null, null, 'Two numbers differ by 7, and the larger is 3 times the smaller minus 5. What is the smaller number?', '["13", "6", "7", "12"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'Let s be the smaller: 3s − 5 − s = 7, so 2s = 12 and s = 6.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2d_014', 'math', 2, 'Algebra', 'Linear inequalities', null, null, 'Which graph description matches the solution set of 5 − x ≥ 2?', '["All numbers greater than 7", "All numbers greater than or equal to 3", "All numbers less than −3", "All numbers less than or equal to 3"]'::jsonb, 3, null, '5 − x ≥ 2 gives −x ≥ −3, so x ≤ 3.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2d_015', 'math', 2, 'Algebra', 'Linear inequalities', null, null, 'A school needs at least $2,000 for a trip. It has $650 and earns $45 per car at a car wash. What is the least number of cars it must wash?', null, null, '["30"]'::jsonb, '650 + 45c ≥ 2,000, so 45c ≥ 1,350 and c ≥ 30.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2d_016', 'math', 2, 'Advanced Math', 'Equivalent expressions', null, null, 'Which expression is equivalent to (x − 3)^{2} − (x + 3)^{2}?', '["−12x", "2x^{2} + 18", "−18", "0"]'::jsonb, 0, null, '(x^{2} − 6x + 9) − (x^{2} + 6x + 9) = −12x.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2d_017', 'math', 2, 'Advanced Math', 'Equivalent expressions', null, null, 'Which expression is a factored form of 3x^{2} − 12?', '["(3x − 2)(x + 6)", "3(x − 4)(x + 4)", "3(x − 2)^{2}", "3(x − 2)(x + 2)"]'::jsonb, 3, null, '3x^{2} − 12 = 3(x^{2} − 4) = 3(x − 2)(x + 2).', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2d_018', 'math', 2, 'Advanced Math', 'Equivalent expressions', null, null, 'If x ≠ 0, which expression is equivalent to (8x^{3} − 4x^{2})/(4x)?', '["2x^{2} − x", "8x^{2} − x", "2x^{3} − x^{2}", "2x^{2} − 4x"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'Divide each term by 4x: 2x^{2} − x.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2d_019', 'math', 2, 'Advanced Math', 'Equivalent expressions', null, null, 'Which expression is equivalent to x^{1/2} · x^{3/2}?', '["x^{3/4}", "x", "x^{2}", "x^{3}"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'Add the exponents: 1/2 + 3/2 = 2.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2d_020', 'math', 2, 'Advanced Math', 'Nonlinear equations', null, null, 'What is the larger solution of x^{2} − 3x − 10 = 0?', null, null, '["5"]'::jsonb, '(x − 5)(x + 2) = 0, so x = 5 or x = −2.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2d_021', 'math', 2, 'Advanced Math', 'Nonlinear equations', null, null, 'If 4^{x} = 64, what is the value of 2^{x}?', '["6", "3", "8", "16"]'::jsonb, 2, null, '4^{x} = 64 gives x = 3, so 2^{3} = 8.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2d_022', 'math', 2, 'Advanced Math', 'Nonlinear equations', null, null, 'If (x + 1)/(x − 2) = 4, what is the value of x?', '["2", "9/5", "3", "1"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'x + 1 = 4x − 8, so 9 = 3x and x = 3.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2d_023', 'math', 2, 'Advanced Math', 'Nonlinear equations', null, null, 'How many real solutions does x^{2} + 9 = 0 have?', '["Two", "Zero", "One", "Infinitely many"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'x^{2} = −9 has no real solution, since a square can''t be negative.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2d_024', 'math', 2, 'Advanced Math', 'Nonlinear functions', null, null, 'The function f is defined by f(x) = (x − 4)^{2} − 1. For what values of x is f(x) = 0?', '["x = 1 and x = 4", "x = −3 and x = −5", "x = 3 and x = 5", "x = 4 only"]'::jsonb, 2, null, '(x − 4)^{2} = 1, so x − 4 = ±1 and x = 3 or 5.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2d_025', 'math', 2, 'Advanced Math', 'Nonlinear functions', null, null, 'A tree''s height, in feet, t years after planting is modeled by h(t) = 6(1.25)^{t}. What was its height when planted?', '["6", "1.25", "7.5", "4.8"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'At t = 0, h(0) = 6(1) = 6.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2d_026', 'math', 2, 'Advanced Math', 'Nonlinear functions', null, null, 'The graph of y = x^{2} + 4x + 1 has its vertex at which x-value?', null, null, '["-2", "−2"]'::jsonb, 'x = −b/(2a) = −4/2 = −2.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2d_027', 'math', 2, 'Advanced Math', 'Nonlinear functions', null, null, 'If f(x) = 3x − 2 and g(x) = x^{2}, what is f(g(−2))?', '["−8", "14", "64", "10"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'g(−2) = 4, and f(4) = 12 − 2 = 10.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2d_028', 'math', 2, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Ratios, rates, and proportions', null, null, 'A 12-ounce bag of coffee costs $9.00 and a 20-ounce bag costs $13.00. How much less does the larger bag cost per ounce, in cents?', '["15", "40", "10", "5"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'Small: 75¢ per ounce. Large: 65¢ per ounce. Difference: 10¢.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2d_029', 'math', 2, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Ratios, rates, and proportions', null, null, 'Light travels about 186,000 miles per second. About how many seconds does it take light to travel 93,000,000 miles from the Sun to Earth?', '["50", "2,000", "5,000", "500"]'::jsonb, 3, null, '93,000,000 ÷ 186,000 = 500 seconds (about 8 minutes).', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2d_030', 'math', 2, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Ratios, rates, and proportions', null, null, 'On a blueprint, 1 inch represents 4 feet. A room is 5.5 inches long on the blueprint. How long is the room, in feet?', null, null, '["22"]'::jsonb, '5.5 × 4 = 22 feet.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2d_031', 'math', 2, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Percentages', null, null, 'A bill of $64 is split so that one friend pays 37.5% and the other pays the rest. How much does the second friend pay, in dollars?', '["24", "37.50", "40", "26.50"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'The second friend pays 62.5% of 64 = 40.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2d_032', 'math', 2, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Percentages', null, null, 'A store''s sales increased from 2,400 items to 3,000 items. What was the percent increase?', '["60%", "20%", "125%", "25%"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'The increase is 600. 600 ÷ 2,400 = 0.25 = 25%.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2d_033', 'math', 2, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Percentages', null, null, 'After a 30% discount, a game costs $42. What was the original price, in dollars?', null, null, '["60"]'::jsonb, '0.70 × P = 42, so P = 60.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2d_034', 'math', 2, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'One-variable data', null, null, 'The dot plot shows the number of siblings of 10 students: 0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 2, 2, 3, 3, 7. Which statement is true?', '["The median is greater than the mean", "The mean equals the median", "The mode is 7", "The mean is greater than the median"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'The median is 1.5 and the mean is 2. The outlier 7 pulls the mean up.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2d_035', 'math', 2, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'One-variable data', null, null, 'Five numbers have a mean of 9. Four of them are 5, 8, 10, and 12. What is the fifth?', '["8", "10", "35", "9"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'The total is 45. 45 − 35 = 10.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2d_036', 'math', 2, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Two-variable data', null, null, 'For a group of runners, the line of best fit y = −0.5x + 30 relates age x (in years, from 20 to 50) to 5K time improvement y (in seconds) after training. What does −0.5 mean?', '["A 30-year-old improves by 0.5 second", "For each additional year of age, the predicted improvement is 0.5 second less", "Improvement increases by 0.5 second per year of age", "Runners get 0.5 second slower each race"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'The slope is the change in predicted y for each 1-year increase in x.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2d_037', 'math', 2, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Two-variable data', null, null, 'Which data set is best modeled by an exponential function?', '["x: 0, 1, 2, 3; y: 40, 30, 20, 10", "x: 0, 1, 2, 3; y: 5, 5, 5, 5", "x: 0, 1, 2, 3; y: 5, 10, 20, 40", "x: 0, 1, 2, 3; y: 5, 10, 15, 20"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'In the set 5, 10, 20, 40, y is multiplied by the same factor (2) at each step, which is exponential. The other sets change by a constant amount or not at all.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2d_038', 'math', 2, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Probability and conditional probability', null, '{"h": ["", "Cats", "Dogs"], "r": [["7th grade", "30", "70"], ["8th grade", "50", "50"]]}'::jsonb, 'A survey of 200 students asked whether they prefer cats or dogs.

If a student who prefers cats is chosen at random, what is the probability the student is in 8th grade?', '["5/8", "3/8", "5/12", "1/4"]'::jsonb, 0, null, '50 + 30 = 80 students prefer cats, and 50 of them are in 8th grade: 50/80 = 5/8.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2d_039', 'math', 2, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Probability and conditional probability', null, null, 'A coin is flipped and a number cube (1–6) is rolled. What is the probability of getting heads and an even number?', '["1/2", "1/4", "1/12", "1/3"]'::jsonb, 1, null, '(1/2) × (3/6) = 1/4.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2d_040', 'math', 2, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Inference from sample statistics', null, null, 'To estimate the average time students at a school spend on homework, which method would most likely produce a biased result?', '["Surveying only students in an advanced math class", "Surveying every 10th student on an alphabetical list", "Surveying random students from each grade", "Surveying a random sample from the whole school"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'Students in one advanced class are not representative of the whole school.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2d_041', 'math', 2, 'Problem-Solving and Data Analysis', 'Inference from sample statistics', null, null, 'A random sample of 300 lightbulbs from a factory found 9 defective. Which is the best estimate of the percent of all bulbs from the factory that are defective?', '["3%", "0.3%", "30%", "9%"]'::jsonb, 0, null, '9 ÷ 300 = 0.03 = 3%.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2d_042', 'math', 2, 'Geometry and Trigonometry', 'Area and volume', null, null, 'A circular garden has a radius of 6 meters. A path 1 meter wide surrounds it. What is the area of the path?', '["12π", "13π", "π", "49π"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'Outer area π(7)^{2} = 49π minus inner area 36π gives 13π.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2d_043', 'math', 2, 'Geometry and Trigonometry', 'Area and volume', null, null, 'The volume of a rectangular box is 210 cubic inches. Its base is 7 inches by 5 inches. What is its height, in inches?', null, null, '["6"]'::jsonb, '210 ÷ (7 × 5) = 6.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2d_044', 'math', 2, 'Geometry and Trigonometry', 'Lines, angles, and triangles', null, null, 'In a parallelogram, one angle measures 65°. What is the measure of an angle next to it?', '["65°", "115°", "25°", "295°"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'Consecutive angles in a parallelogram are supplementary: 180 − 65 = 115.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2d_045', 'math', 2, 'Geometry and Trigonometry', 'Lines, angles, and triangles', null, null, 'A tree casts a 15-foot shadow at the same time a 6-foot person casts a 4-foot shadow. How tall is the tree, in feet?', '["17", "22.5", "60", "10"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'The triangles are similar: 6/4 = h/15, so h = 22.5.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2d_046', 'math', 2, 'Geometry and Trigonometry', 'Right triangles and trigonometry', null, null, 'In right triangle ABC with right angle C, AC = 7 and AB = 25. What is cos A?', '["25/7", "7/24", "24/25", "7/25"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'cos A = adjacent ÷ hypotenuse = AC/AB = 7/25.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2d_047', 'math', 2, 'Geometry and Trigonometry', 'Right triangles and trigonometry', null, null, 'A wheelchair ramp rises 2 feet over a horizontal run of 24 feet. What is the slope of the ramp, as a fraction?', '["1/24", "1/2", "1/12", "12"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'Rise ÷ run = 2/24 = 1/12.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2d_048', 'math', 2, 'Geometry and Trigonometry', 'Circles', null, null, 'Which point lies on the circle x^{2} + y^{2} = 25?', '["(3, −4)", "(0, 25)", "(2, 3)", "(5, 5)"]'::jsonb, 0, null, '3^{2} + (−4)^{2} = 9 + 16 = 25.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('mathl2d_049', 'math', 2, 'Geometry and Trigonometry', 'Circles', null, null, 'A circle has circumference 30π. What is its area?', '["225π", "30π", "15π", "900π"]'::jsonb, 0, null, '2πr = 30π gives r = 15, so the area is 225π.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_001', 'rw', 1, 'Craft and Structure', 'Words in Context', 'The firefighter was praised for being ____. She ran back into the smoky building to rescue a family''s frightened cat.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?', '["lazy", "clumsy", "brave", "timid"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'Running into danger to help others shows courage, which is what brave means.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_002', 'rw', 1, 'Craft and Structure', 'Words in Context', 'The blue whale is ____. It can grow longer than three school buses parked end to end.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?', '["delicate", "tiny", "narrow", "enormous"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'A creature longer than three school buses is enormous.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_003', 'rw', 1, 'Craft and Structure', 'Words in Context', 'Birdwatchers must be ____. They often wait quietly for hours just to catch a glimpse of a rare bird.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?', '["patient", "rushed", "careless", "grumpy"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'Waiting calmly for hours shows patience.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_004', 'rw', 1, 'Craft and Structure', 'Words in Context', 'In the fall, farmers ____ their pumpkins, cutting them from the vines once they turn bright orange.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?', '["sell", "plant", "water", "harvest"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'Gathering ripe crops is called the harvest.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_005', 'rw', 1, 'Craft and Structure', 'Words in Context', 'Robin eggs are so ____ that even a light tap can crack their thin blue shells.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?', '["heavy", "fragile", "plain", "sturdy"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'Eggs that break easily are fragile.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_006', 'rw', 1, 'Craft and Structure', 'Words in Context', 'The new backpack is so light that Kayla barely notices it, even when it holds all of her books.', null, 'As used in the text, what does the word "light" most nearly mean?', '["to set on fire", "not heavy", "pale in color", "bright"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'The text is about how easy the backpack is to carry, so "light" means not heavy.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_007', 'rw', 1, 'Craft and Structure', 'Words in Context', 'Using a hand lens, the students ____ the ants as they carry crumbs back to their nest.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?', '["forget", "ignore", "break", "observe"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'Watching carefully to learn is what observe means.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_008', 'rw', 1, 'Craft and Structure', 'Words in Context', 'The crowd was ____ by the magician''s final trick and clapped and cheered for several minutes.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?', '["sleepy", "puzzled", "delighted", "upset"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'Clapping and cheering show that the crowd was very happy, or delighted.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_009', 'rw', 1, 'Craft and Structure', 'Text Structure and Purpose', 'Bees collect a sweet liquid called nectar from flowers. Back at the hive, they pass the nectar to other bees and store it in wax cells. The bees fan the nectar with their wings until most of the water evaporates, turning it into thick honey.', null, 'Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?', '["To explain how bees make honey", "To argue that people should eat more honey", "To describe different kinds of flowers", "To compare bees and wasps"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'The text describes the steps bees follow to turn nectar into honey.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_010', 'rw', 1, 'Craft and Structure', 'Text Structure and Purpose', 'Recycling paper helps protect the environment. It saves trees from being cut down. It also uses less water and energy than making new paper from wood.', null, 'Which choice best describes the function of the first sentence in the overall structure of the text?', '["It states the main idea that the rest of the text supports", "It disagrees with the second sentence", "It gives a detail that is not related to the rest", "It asks a question the text never answers"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'The first sentence says recycling paper helps the environment; the rest gives reasons.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_011', 'rw', 1, 'Craft and Structure', 'Text Structure and Purpose', 'A monarch butterfly begins life as a tiny egg on a milkweed leaf. A few days later, a caterpillar hatches and starts eating. After about two weeks, it forms a green chrysalis. Finally, an adult butterfly breaks out and spreads its orange wings.', null, 'Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?', '["It compares two animals", "It lists unrelated facts", "It describes events in the order they happened", "It argues for one opinion"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'The text follows the caterpillar''s life in time order: egg, caterpillar, chrysalis, butterfly.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_012', 'rw', 1, 'Craft and Structure', 'Cross-Text Connections', 'Text 1
School gardens teach students about science, such as how plants grow and what soil needs.

Text 2
Students who help grow vegetables in school gardens are more willing to try eating them, too.', null, 'Based on the texts, how would the author of Text 2 most likely respond to Text 1?', '["By saying that students dislike vegetables", "By agreeing that school gardens are useful and adding another benefit", "By arguing that schools should remove their gardens", "By claiming that gardens cost too much"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'Both authors support gardens; Text 2 adds that students try more vegetables.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_013', 'rw', 1, 'Craft and Structure', 'Cross-Text Connections', 'Text 1
On a clear day, the sky looks blue.

Text 2
Sunlight is made of many colors. As it passes through the air, blue light is scattered in all directions much more than other colors, so we see blue everywhere we look.', null, 'Which choice best describes how the two texts are related?', '["Text 2 explains the reason for the fact in Text 1", "Text 1 tells a story and Text 2 tells a joke", "Both texts are about different topics", "Text 2 disagrees with Text 1"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'Text 1 states that the sky is blue; Text 2 explains why.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_014', 'rw', 1, 'Information and Ideas', 'Central Ideas and Details', 'Cactuses can survive months without rain. Instead of wide leaves, which would lose water, they have sharp spines. Their thick stems store water like sponges, and their shallow, spreading roots quickly soak up rain when it does fall.', null, 'Which choice best states the main idea of the text?', '["Cactuses grow best in rainforests", "Cactuses have features that help them survive in dry deserts", "Cactuses need water every day", "Cactuses have large, flat leaves"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'The text lists features that help cactuses save and collect water in the desert.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_015', 'rw', 1, 'Information and Ideas', 'Central Ideas and Details', 'On April 15, 1947, Jackie Robinson took the field for the Brooklyn Dodgers, becoming the first African American to play in modern Major League Baseball. Today, every player in the league wears his number, 42, on April 15 to honor him.', null, 'According to the text, why did Jackie Robinson become famous in 1947?', '["He invented a new kind of baseball bat", "He won the Olympic gold medal", "He became the first African American to play in modern Major League Baseball", "He became the coach of a college team"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'The text says he broke baseball''s color line in 1947.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_016', 'rw', 1, 'Information and Ideas', 'Central Ideas and Details', 'Last November, the fifth graders at Pine Hill School organized a food drive. They made posters, set up collection boxes, and gathered more than 600 cans of food. They donated everything to a local food bank that helps families in need.', null, 'Which choice best states the main idea of the text?', '["Canned food is not healthy", "Most families have plenty of food", "Food drives are only for adults", "Kids can help their community by organizing a food drive"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'The text describes how students collected food for families in need.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_017', 'rw', 1, 'Information and Ideas', 'Central Ideas and Details', 'When Omar looked out the window and saw the yard covered in fresh snow, he jumped out of bed, shouted for his sister, and raced to find his boots.', null, 'Based on the text, how does Omar feel when he sees the snow?', '["Frightened", "Angry", "Bored", "Excited"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'Omar jumps out of bed and races to get his boots, showing excitement.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_018', 'rw', 1, 'Information and Ideas', 'Command of Evidence', 'A student recorded the high temperature for four days. The table shows that ____.', '{"h": ["Day", "High (°F)"], "r": [["Monday", "70"], ["Tuesday", "78"], ["Wednesday", "72"], ["Thursday", "65"]]}'::jsonb, 'Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to complete the statement?', '["Thursday was warmer than Tuesday", "Tuesday was the warmest day of the week shown", "Monday was the warmest day", "all days had the same temperature"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'Tuesday''s 78°F is higher than any other day in the table.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_019', 'rw', 1, 'Information and Ideas', 'Command of Evidence', 'A teacher claims that the new reading corner helped students read more.', null, 'Which finding would best support the claim that the new reading corner helped students read more?', '["Some students prefer to read at home", "Students checked out more books each week after the reading corner opened than before", "The reading corner has bean bag chairs", "The reading corner is painted blue"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'Only this finding compares reading before and after the reading corner opened.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_020', 'rw', 1, 'Information and Ideas', 'Command of Evidence', 'In a story, Grace is nervous before giving a speech.', null, 'Which quotation from the story best shows that Grace is nervous?', '["\"Grace wore her favorite blue dress.\"", "\"Grace''s voice shook as she began her speech, and she gripped her note cards tightly.\"", "\"Grace had written her speech about dolphins.\"", "\"Grace''s class sat in the front row.\""]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'A shaking voice and tight grip show nervousness.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_021', 'rw', 1, 'Information and Ideas', 'Command of Evidence', 'A coach claims that the soccer team improved over the season.', '{"h": ["Game", "Goals scored"], "r": [["1", "2"], ["2", "3"], ["3", "4"], ["4", "6"]]}'::jsonb, 'Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to support the claim?', '["The team played four games", "The team scored 2 goals in its first game and 6 goals in its last game", "The team scored 4 goals in its third game", "Soccer is a popular sport"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'The claim is that the team improved; comparing first and last games shows this.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_022', 'rw', 1, 'Information and Ideas', 'Inferences', 'When Lena entered the den, she found a warm mug of cocoa on the table and a book lying open on the couch. She realized that ____', null, 'Which choice most logically completes the text?', '["the room had been empty for years", "it was the middle of the night", "the lamp was broken", "someone had recently been in the room"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'A warm mug and an open book are clues that someone was just there.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_023', 'rw', 1, 'Information and Ideas', 'Inferences', 'The soil in the flowerpot was dry and cracked, and the plant''s leaves were drooping toward the floor. It seemed that ____', null, 'Which choice most logically completes the text?', '["the plant is growing too fast", "the plant needs water", "the plant gets too much sunlight", "the plant has new flowers"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'Dry soil and drooping leaves are signs the plant is thirsty.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_024', 'rw', 1, 'Information and Ideas', 'Inferences', 'Rain poured down all afternoon, and by four o''clock the soccer field was covered in puddles. The coach sent a message telling all the players to stay home. The players guessed that ____', null, 'Which choice most logically completes the text?', '["the game would start early", "the team had already won", "the game had been canceled because of the storm", "the field had been painted"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'Heavy rain, a flooded field, and the coach sending everyone home suggest a cancellation.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_025', 'rw', 1, 'Information and Ideas', 'Inferences', 'Kai tested a magnet on several objects. It picked up paper clips and iron nails, but it did not pick up a copper coin or a piece of aluminum foil. Kai concluded that ____', null, 'Which choice most logically completes the text?', '["magnets attract only plastic", "magnets attract every object", "magnets attract some metals but not others", "magnets do not work in water"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'The magnet picked up the paper clips and nails but not the coin or foil, so it attracts only some metals.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_026', 'rw', 1, 'Standard English Conventions', 'Boundaries', 'Our class took a trip to the ____ giraffes were our favorite animals.', null, 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["zoo and, the", "zoo the", "zoo. The", "zoo, the"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'These are two complete sentences, so a period separates them.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_027', 'rw', 1, 'Standard English Conventions', 'Boundaries', 'Please bring these ____ erasers, and a ruler.', null, 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["supplies pencils,", "supplies, pencils:", "supplies: pencils,", "supplies; pencils,"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'A colon introduces the list after a complete sentence.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_028', 'rw', 1, 'Standard English Conventions', 'Boundaries', 'Sally ____ physicist and astronaut, became the first American woman in space in 1983.', null, 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["Ride; a", "Ride. A", "Ride a", "Ride, a"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'The phrase "a physicist and astronaut" describes Sally Ride and is set off with commas.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_029', 'rw', 1, 'Standard English Conventions', 'Boundaries', 'The campers were ____ they cooked hot dogs over the fire.', null, 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["hungry, so", "hungry so", "hungry. So,", "hungry; so,"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'A comma comes before "so" when it joins two complete sentences.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_030', 'rw', 1, 'Standard English Conventions', 'Boundaries', 'The little brown ____ chased the ball across the yard.', null, 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["dog,", "dog;", "dog", "dog:"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'No punctuation belongs between the subject "The little brown dog" and its verb.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_031', 'rw', 1, 'Standard English Conventions', 'Boundaries', 'Saturday was warm and ____ Sunday was cold and rainy.', null, 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["sunny,", "sunny;", "sunny", "sunny:"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'A semicolon joins two complete sentences.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_032', 'rw', 1, 'Standard English Conventions', 'Form, Structure, and Sense', 'The books on the top shelf ____ about space and planets.', null, 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["are", "was", "is", "has been"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'The subject "the books" is plural, so the verb is "are."', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_033', 'rw', 1, 'Standard English Conventions', 'Form, Structure, and Sense', 'Grandma showed us how to knit with ____ old wooden needles.', null, 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["his", "its", "their", "her"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'The pronoun refers to "Grandma," so "her" is correct.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_034', 'rw', 1, 'Standard English Conventions', 'Form, Structure, and Sense', 'In 1869, workers in Utah ____ a golden spike to complete the first railroad across the United States.', null, 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["drives", "will drive", "is driving", "drove"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'The sentence describes an event in 1869, so the past tense is needed.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_035', 'rw', 1, 'Standard English Conventions', 'Form, Structure, and Sense', 'The coach washed all of the ____ uniforms after the big game.', null, 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["players", "playeres", "players''", "player''s"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'The uniforms belong to many players, so the plural possessive "players''" is correct.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_036', 'rw', 1, 'Standard English Conventions', 'Form, Structure, and Sense', 'Everyone in the choir ____ the national anthem before the game.', null, 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["have sung", "sing", "singing", "sings"]'::jsonb, 3, null, '"Everyone" is singular, so the verb is "sings."', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_037', 'rw', 1, 'Standard English Conventions', 'Form, Structure, and Sense', 'My cousin shared her popcorn with ____ at the movies.', null, 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["me", "I", "my", "mine"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'The pronoun is the object of "with," so "me" is correct.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_038', 'rw', 1, 'Expression of Ideas', 'Transitions', 'Most birds can fly. ____ penguins, ostriches, and emus cannot.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?', '["However,", "For example,", "Similarly,", "Therefore,"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'The second sentence contrasts with the first.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_039', 'rw', 1, 'Expression of Ideas', 'Transitions', 'To make a smoothie, first put fruit and yogurt in a blender. ____ blend everything until it is smooth.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?', '["However,", "Then,", "In contrast,", "For example,"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'The steps happen in order, so "Then" fits.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_040', 'rw', 1, 'Expression of Ideas', 'Transitions', 'Lucia saved her allowance every week for six months. ____ she was able to buy the new bike she wanted.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?', '["As a result,", "However,", "For example,", "Meanwhile,"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'Saving her money led to buying the bike, so a result transition fits.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_041', 'rw', 1, 'Expression of Ideas', 'Transitions', 'Several planets in our solar system have rings. ____ Saturn has bright rings made of ice and rock.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?', '["For example,", "However,", "Finally,", "As a result,"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'The second sentence gives an example of a planet with rings.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_042', 'rw', 1, 'Expression of Ideas', 'Transitions', 'Drinking water helps your body stay cool. ____ it helps carry nutrients to your cells.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?', '["In addition,", "However,", "In contrast,", "Instead,"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'The second sentence adds another benefit.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_043', 'rw', 1, 'Expression of Ideas', 'Rhetorical Synthesis', 'While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:
• Koalas live in eastern Australia.
• They eat almost only eucalyptus leaves.
• An adult can eat up to a pound of leaves a day.
• They sleep up to 20 hours a day.
• Baby koalas are called joeys.', null, 'The student wants to describe what koalas eat. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?', '["Koalas eat almost nothing but eucalyptus leaves, munching up to a pound of them a day.", "Koalas live in Australia.", "Koalas sleep up to 20 hours a day.", "Baby koalas are called joeys."]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'Only this choice describes the koala''s diet.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_044', 'rw', 1, 'Expression of Ideas', 'Rhetorical Synthesis', 'While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:
• Mary Anderson was born in Alabama in 1866.
• She visited New York City in 1902.
• She noticed drivers struggling to see through snowy windows.
• In 1903, she patented a hand-operated windshield wiper.
• She also ran a cattle ranch.', null, 'The student wants to explain what Mary Anderson invented. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?', '["Mary Anderson visited New York City in 1902.", "Mary Anderson was born in Alabama.", "Mary Anderson invented the windshield wiper, a hand-operated arm that cleared rain and snow from a car''s front window.", "Mary Anderson ran a cattle ranch."]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'Only this choice describes what she invented.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1d_045', 'rw', 1, 'Expression of Ideas', 'Rhetorical Synthesis', 'While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:
• The Sun and the Moon both appear in our sky.
• The Sun is a star.
• The Sun makes its own light.
• The Moon does not make its own light.
• The Moon reflects light from the Sun.', null, 'The student wants to show a difference between the Sun and the Moon. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?', '["The Sun and the Moon both appear in the sky.", "The Moon orbits Earth.", "The Sun is a star.", "The Sun makes its own light, while the Moon only reflects light from the Sun."]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'Only this choice states a difference.', 'published', 'import', now())
on conflict (id) do nothing;
